## Baking Memory — protocol

Cross-repo / cross-session decisions live in **`~/.cursor/baking/memory/baking-memory.db`** (SQLite FTS). Same store for Cursor and Claude Code. CLI: `baking memory …` · spec: `~/Desktop/side/baking/MEMORY.md`.

Active when `lightStack.memory.provider` is `"baking"` in config.

### WHEN TO SAVE (mandatory — not optional)

Run `baking memory save` after any of these:

- Bug fix completed
- Architecture or design decision made
- Non-obvious discovery about the codebase
- Configuration change or environment setup
- Pattern established (naming, structure, convention)
- User preference or constraint learned

Format:

```bash
baking memory save \
  --topic "<project>/<slug>" \
  --title "Verb + what — short, searchable" \
  --body "**What**: … **Why**: … **Where**: … **Learned**: …" \
  --type decision \
  --project "<repo-slug>"
```

Types: `decision` · `session` · `architecture` · `discovery` · `pattern`

Reuse the same `--topic` to update an evolving decision (new row; search by topic).

### WHEN TO SEARCH

When the user asks to recall past work — "remember", "recall", "recordar", "qué hicimos", etc.:

1. `baking memory context --query "<terms>"` (recent + relevant)
2. If weak, `baking memory search "<keywords>"`

Also search **proactively** when starting work that may have been decided in another repo or session.

### SESSION CLOSE (mandatory for non-trivial Baking runs)

Before "done" / "listo", save a session summary:

```bash
baking memory save \
  --type session \
  --title "Session summary" \
  --body "## Goal\n…\n## Discoveries\n- …\n## Accomplished\n- …\n## Next Steps\n- …"
```

Five bullets minimum. Skipping this leaves the next session blind.

### DON'T

- Dump whole handoffs or READMEs into memory
- Save every chat turn — only durable decisions and conventions
